== Biography ==

A Scottish baptism index records a '''John Glasgow''' at Glasgow in August 1782. The original register has not been inspected, and the index date should not automatically be treated as a birth date.<ref>“Scotland, Births and Baptisms, 1564–1950,” FamilySearch, [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:X1WW-W8Z John Glasgow, 1782]; citation carried from former Glasgow-3054.</ref>

A Find a Grave memorial reports that a John Glasgow died in January 1848 and was buried at Southern Necropolis, Glasgow. It gives an approximate birth year of 1783, but no grave photograph was available when the earlier profile was reviewed. The death and burial require independent confirmation.<ref name="FAG245479765">{{FindAGrave|245479765|sameas=no}}</ref>

== Research Notes ==

The former Glasgow-3054 and this profile were combined as the leading match: the baptism and memorial name a John Glasgow of Glasgow, with birth-year information differing by only about one year. Neither index supplies a parent, spouse or other continuous identifier joining the 1782 child to the 1848 deceased, so the later-life identification remains provisional. The 1782 index is the more specific early event; the memorial's circa 1783 is an estimate, not an independently documented competing baptism.

[[Glasgow-2952|John Glasgow of St Vincent]] is a different candidate sometimes mentioned in the earlier profile. His death by 1817 is incompatible with a Glasgow burial in 1848; his plantation family should not be merged into this profile.

